				"⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿",
				99,
				108
			],
			"Message": "chore(Output): Remove Configuration directory from Output element\n\nDelete all configuration files from the Output element including ESBuild configs (Editor, Exclude, Microsoft, Output, RestPlugin), Plugin configs (Apply, Copy, Index, Transform, Type), Polyfill configs (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPCRenderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcess), Service configs (DevLog, TauriMainProcess, Trace), and tsconfig files.\n\nThis removes the inline build configuration, likely to be replaced with externalized or generated configuration files.",
			"SHA": "1060f224e9bdb62f9ed92e98b59af69ea482117a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T22:55:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				224,
				10
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add DisableUnusedServices transform and fix ExtensionScannerIPC path matching\n\nAdd a new DisableUnusedServices ESBuild transform that replaces upstream VS Code contribution barrels for features Land doesn't back (auto-update, issue reporter, MS account/sync, process explorer) with inert stubs. This removes broken UI surfaces, silences \"service not registered\" warnings, and shortens boot time.\n\nAlso fix ExtensionScannerIPC to match BOTH the electron-browser and browser variants of extensionsScannerService.js. Previously the regex only matched electron-browser, but the desktop.main.js profile loads the browser variant. Both paths now route to Mountain for extension scanning.\n\nThe BuildPipeline now includes DisableUnusedServices as step 18, following ExposeWorkbenchAccessor.",
			"SHA": "472589f784e2d779c6a00b5ab53b558cc554ac57"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T22:35:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				2
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "594ca5f4b29277d2c2e8b3be8df850061d799c68"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T22:35:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				221,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Patch desktop.main.js in addition to web.main.js\n\nExtend the ExposeWorkbenchAccessor ESBuild transform to also patch the Electron/Desktop profile's desktop.main.js entry point, not just the web profile's web.main.js. Both files contain the identical instantiation service startup line, but have different first-import markers - web.main.js uses the 'mark' import from performance.js while desktop.main.js uses localize from nls.js. Extract the shared service decorator imports into SharedImportLines to avoid duplication, and add DesktopMainImportMarker/DesktopMainImportReplacement pairs. The match pattern and transform logic are extended to handle both /vs/workbench/browser/web.main.js and /vs/workbench/electron-browser/desktop.main.js. This ensures __CEL_SERVICES__ is populated correctly for the debug-electron and release-electron profiles used at runtime, not just the web profile.",
			"SHA": "11093ba8d18c074bbc8d08572454d6eb96304797"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1782748848362
}